            view: 'Two real assets that the reported return completely hides. **Indoco is the category leader in Indian stomatologicals — dental — which is a genuine niche monopoly rather than a marketing claim**, alongside a top-five brand set led by Cyclopam approaching ₹200cr with the switching costs decades of prescriber habit create. Separately, **European approvals at Baddi and Goa support a contract book for EU customers that is entirely independent of the US problem** and does not depend on Goa Plant 1 clearing. Divesting the domestic ophthalmic division was the right call: it deleveraged and sharpened focus onto exactly these two franchises.',
